Hmm wait — undo should be itself recorded so trail shows it? If undo pushes to future a "撤销" entry, then redo would... getting complicated. Simpler classic model:
- past: stack of {meta, state}
- present: current state (implicit)
- future: stack of {meta, state}
- undo(): future.unshift({meta:{seq:++seq,label:"撤销 · "+topLabel}, state:snapshot()}); state = past.pop().state;
- redo(): past.push({meta:{seq:++seq,label:"重做 · "+future[0].meta.label.replace("撤销 · ","")}, state: snapshot()}); state = future.shift().state;
- reset(): mutate({label:"复位到初始视图", tag:"复位"}, () => { state = clone(INITIAL); }) — keeps reset undoable. Good (recoverable).
- Trail display: newest-first list = [...past].reverse().map(n=>n.meta) plus a "当前" marker? Display past (reversed, newest at top) + future (as muted "可重做" entries)? Trail shows past entries only + current state label? For click-to-jump: each trail row corresponds to a past index; clicking = jump there: take node at index i: future.unshift(current snapshot...), state = node.state, past = past.slice(0, i). Let me implement jumpTo(i):
